Command: ./scripts/openroad_docker.sh (make openroad), then
         ./scripts/orfs_liberty_check.sh
Config: flow/designs/nangate45/muse_crypto/{config.mk,constraint.sdc}
  CORE_UTILIZATION=28, CLOCK_PERIOD=10ns (100 MHz constraint),
  EARLY_SIZING_CAP_RATIO=0.8,
  SDC set_max_capacitance 21 fF (repair guardband, not signoff),
  DONT_USE_CELLS += NOR3_X1 NOR4_X1 NOR4_X2 AOI221_X1 OAI221_X1.
Scope: crypto accelerator macro only (muse_crypto_top, current .sv
sources). This is GDS generated / place-and-route complete for
that macro; it is not a tapeout, not full-SoC closure (#11), and
says nothing about core timing (the in-house core is not in
this macro).

Two runs were made for #31:
  rerun1 = b3 cell ban unchanged. Timing closed, but liberty
           signoff found 3 new max-capacitance violators.
  rerun2 = + AOI221_X1 OAI221_X1 in DONT_USE_CELLS (the two
           violating cell types: OAI221_X1 limit 22.16 fF,
           AOI221_X1 limit 13.81 fF). Clean; this is the
           released run. Fresh run from cleaned ORFS outputs,
           so placement is not identical to b3 or rerun1.

