Conclusion: at the 10 ns (100 MHz) constraint the macro closes
setup and hold with TNS 0 and no liberty, route-DRC or antenna
violations. The +2.9% die / +3.1% stdcell-count growth vs b3 is
a fresh-run + banned-cell effect, not an RTL change (crypto RTL
is behavior-identical .sv since #19).
